          className={`inline-block size-2 rounded-full ${
            connected ? "bg-green-500" : "bg-red-500"
          }`}
        />
        <span className="hidden md:inline">
          {connected ? "ws connected" : "ws disconnected"}
        </span>
      </span>

      <span className="text-muted-foreground hidden md:inline">|</span>

      {/* Agent status - compact on mobile */}
      <span className="hidden md:inline">agent: {STATUS_LABELS[status]}</span>
      <span className="md:hidden text-[10px]">{STATUS_LABELS[status]}</span>

      <span className="text-muted-foreground hidden md:inline">|</span>

      <div className="flex items-center gap-1.5">
        {onToggleRaw && (
          <button
            onClick={onToggleRaw}
            className={cn(
              "rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-mono transition-colors",
              showRaw
                ? "bg-foreground text-background"
                : "bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/80"
            )}
          >
            {showRaw ? "RAW" : "raw"}
          </button>
        )}
        {onToggleTasks && (
          <Button
            variant="ghost"
            size="icon-xs"
            onClick={onToggleTasks}
            title="Toggle tasks"
            className={cn(showTasks && "text-primary")}
          >
            <ListTodo className="size-3.5" />
          </Button>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
);
```

**What changed:**
- Added `Menu` icon import from lucide-react.
- Hamburger button: `md:hidden` so it only shows below 768px.
- "thos dashboard" label: full text hidden on mobile (`hidden md:inline`), replaced with shortened "thos" (`md:hidden`).
- WS status text: `hidden md:inline` -- on mobile, only the green/red dot shows.
- Pipe separators: `hidden md:inline`.
- Agent status: full text on desktop, compact `text-[10px]` on mobile.
- Horizontal padding reduced: `px-2 md:px-4`.
- Gap between right-side items reduced on mobile: `gap-1.5 md:gap-3`.

---

### File 4: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/agent-sidebar.tsx`

**Changes needed:** Minimal. The sidebar component itself does not need to know it is inside a drawer -- the drawer behavior is handled by its parent wrapper in `page.tsx`. However, one adjustment is important:

**Add `h-full` and `bg-sidebar` to ensure it fills the drawer and has a proper background when overlaid:**

```tsx
// Line 163 - the root div. Before:
<div className="flex w-56 flex-col border-r bg-sidebar text-sidebar-foreground">

// After:
<div className="flex h-full w-56 flex-col border-r bg-sidebar text-sidebar-foreground">
```

The `h-full` ensures the sidebar stretches the full height of the fixed-position drawer container. The `bg-sidebar` is already present (good -- it needs an opaque background for the overlay to work correctly).

No other changes are needed in this file. The context menu already uses `fixed z-50` positioning, so it will work correctly in the drawer context.

---

### File 5: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/task-panel.tsx`

**Changes needed:** Minimal, similar to sidebar. The drawer wrapping is handled by the parent. One small adjustment:

```tsx
// Line 41 - root div. Before:
<div className="flex h-full flex-col">

// This is already correct -- `h-full` fills the drawer container.
// No changes needed.
```

The `TaskPanel` already has `h-full` and its `onClose` callback is already wired up. The parent `page.tsx` already handles closing the task panel and auto-closing on agent selection.

**Optional enhancement -- add `bg-background` if not inherited:**

The task panel's root `div` does not explicitly set a background. On desktop this is fine because it inherits from the page background. On mobile, when it is `fixed` overlaying content, it needs an explicit background. This is handled in the parent wrapper:

```tsx
// In page.tsx, the task panel wrapper already includes:
"bg-background"
```

So no changes to `task-panel.tsx` are strictly needed.

---

### File 6: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/message.tsx`

**Changes needed:** One small adjustment to message bubble max-width on mobile for better readability:

```tsx
// Before:
"max-w-[80%] rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap",

// After:
"max-w-[90%] md:max-w-[80%] rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap",
```

On mobile, 80% of a small screen is quite narrow. Allowing 90% gives more room for message content while still keeping the directional alignment clear.

---

### File 7: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/control-request.tsx`

**Changes needed:** Reduce max-width constraint on mobile:

```tsx
// Before:
<div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-muted-foreground/30 p-4">

// After:
<div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-muted-foreground/30 p-3 md:p-4">
```

Slightly tighter padding on mobile. The `max-w-lg` (32rem = 512px) will naturally be constrained by the screen width on mobile, so no responsive change needed there.

---

### File 8: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/user-question.tsx`

**Same pattern as control-request:**

```tsx
// Before:
<div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg space-y-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-muted-foreground/30 p-4">

// After:
<div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg space-y-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-muted-foreground/30 p-3 md:p-4">
```

---

### No Changes Needed

The following files require **no changes**:
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/app/globals.css` -- No custom media queries needed. Tailwind v4's `md:` prefix handles everything.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/app/layout.tsx` -- Viewport meta tag is handled by Next.js automatically.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/lib/utils.ts` -- `cn()` utility already works perfectly for conditional class merging.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/ui/button.tsx` -- Button sizes are already appropriate for touch.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/condensed-tool-group.tsx` -- Already works at any width.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/task-card.tsx` -- Already responsive (uses `truncate`, `flex-wrap` etc).
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/task-create-form.tsx` -- Already full-width within its container.
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/server/ws.ts` -- Server-side, unrelated.

---

### Implementation Order

1. **`app/dashboard/page.tsx`** -- Add `sidebarOpen` state, drawer wrappers, backdrops. This is the structural foundation that everything else depends on.
2. **`components/dashboard/status-bar.tsx`** -- Add hamburger button and responsive layout. This connects the sidebar toggle to the UI.
3. **`components/dashboard/chat.tsx`** -- Accept `onToggleSidebar` prop, pass it to StatusBar, adjust padding.
4. **`components/dashboard/agent-sidebar.tsx`** -- Add `h-full` to root.
5. **`components/dashboard/message.tsx`** -- Adjust `max-w` for mobile.
6. **`components/dashboard/control-request.tsx`** and **`components/dashboard/user-question.tsx`** -- Minor padding adjustments (can be done together).

---

### Potential Pitfalls and Mitigations

**Context menu positioning in sidebar drawer:** The context menu in `AgentSidebar` uses `fixed` positioning with `clientX`/`clientY` coordinates. Since the sidebar drawer is also `fixed`, and the context menu uses viewport-relative coordinates from `getBoundingClientRect()` and `clientX/Y`, this will work correctly without changes. The `z-50` on the menu matches the drawer's `z-50`, but since the menu is a child of the drawer DOM, it will render on top.

**Task panel width on very small screens:** The `max-w-[calc(100vw-3rem)]` on the task panel wrapper ensures it never exceeds screen width minus a 48px gap. The inner `w-80` (320px) will be constrained by this max. On phones narrower than 368px, the panel shrinks gracefully. The `TaskCreateForm` and `TaskCard` components already use `w-full` and relative sizing inside, so they will adapt.

**Scroll locking when drawers are open:** The `overflow-hidden` on the root container and the backdrop `onClick` handler are sufficient. No need for `body` scroll locking since the entire app is contained within `h-dvh`.

**Transition on task panel:** The task panel uses conditional rendering (`{showTasks && ...}`), so it will not have a slide-in animation -- it will pop in. If a slide animation is desired later, the task panel wrapper would need to always be rendered (like the sidebar) and use `translate-x-full` / `translate-x-0` toggling. For now, the simpler conditional render approach matches the existing behavior and avoids unnecessary complexity.

---

### Critical Files for Implementation
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/app/dashboard/page.tsx` - Core layout orchestrator: add sidebar state, drawer wrappers, backdrop overlays
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/status-bar.tsx` - Add hamburger menu button and responsive class changes for compact mobile layout
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/chat.tsx` - Wire onToggleSidebar prop through to StatusBar, adjust padding for mobile
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/agent-sidebar.tsx` - Add h-full to root element for proper drawer height
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/message.tsx` - Widen message bubbles on mobile (90% vs 80%)

